    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0414" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/703.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Hill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department acknowledges your dispatch
                    of the 21st ultimo, in which you inclosed in duplicate a translation of a note
                    received on that date from the German foreign office relative to the proposed
                    opium conference, stating that the German Government is glad to accept the
                    suggestion of the United States in the matter of the conference, and in common
                    with other Governments of the powers who took part in the International Opium
                    Commission <pb facs="0415" n="303" xml:id="pg303"/> at Shanghai, to send
                    full-powered delegates to a conference, in order to reach an international
                    agreement based on the findings of the above-mentioned commission, and that the
                    program submitted by the United States as a basis for a previous exchange of
                    opinion, will be taken into consideration by the German Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. Knox</signed>.)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Huntington Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
